{{Quote|I need to find a new hang glider to explore the Surabat River Valley. Can you help me?|Peekpa's job posting|<ref name="Datapad">[[Star Wars: Datapad|''Star Wars'': Datapad]]</ref>}}
'''Surabat River Valley''' was a location on the [[planet]] [[Batuu]]<ref name="Traveler's Guide" /> that was named after the settler of the planet, [[Ariana Surabat]],<ref name="GEStaff">[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge|''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge]] has official backstory elements that, though not directly published for the public, are officially canon details that can be obtained verbally from cast members working in the land.</ref> who laid down her flag in the valley upon her first arrival on the planet.<ref name="Myths and Fables">{{StoryCite|story=The Skiff & the Galleons|book=Myths & Fables}}</ref> The deep, curved valley was full of tall, pointed spires of rock that proved difficult for [[pilot]]s to navigate through, many of which required very treacherous turns.<ref name="Map">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-galaxys-edge-black-spire-exclusive-excerpt|text=Leia Has a Mission for Vi Moradi in ''Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge - Black Spire'' - Exclusive Excerpt}}</ref> The [[Surabat]] vicinity was located in the valley.<ref name="Traveler's Guide" />

At some point after the [[Battle of Crait]] during the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]], the [[Ewok]] [[Peekpa]] hoped to explore the river valley while on Batuu. She posted a job listing in [[Black Spire Outpost]] requesting that someone help her find a new [[Hang-glider|hang glider]] to explore the valley with. A visitor to the outpost responded, and successfully located the glider at [[Outer Rim Expedition and Supply]], which Peekpa claimed she would pick up and use later on.<ref name="Datapad" />

==Behind the scenes==
The valley was first depicted in [[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge trading cards|trading cards]] released on [[December 16]], [[2017]] at [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney's]] "Galactic Nights" session, an event that previewed locations and details from the then-upcoming themed land [[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge|''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge]]. Similar to other map cards, the card containing the valley contained part of an [[Aurebesh]] poem along the border of the card. However, unlike the other cards, it has two Aurebesh lines, due to it being a corner card. The lines were, for the bottom line "COME STAY FOREVER OR", and for the left line, "JUST PASS ON THROUGH".<ref name="Inside the Magic">{{WebCite|url=https://insidethemagic.net/2018/05/full-star-wars-galaxys-edge-area-map-more-location-names-revealed-by-trading-card-set-at-walt-disney-world|text=Full Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge area map, more location names revealed by trading card set at Walt Disney World|author=Celestino, Mike|date=2018-05-29|archivedate=20200122190633}}</ref>

